<Docs title="Production deployment"><div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">OPERATE / PRODUCTION</span><h1>Deploy a boundary you can trust.</h1><p>Docker and Kubernetes are the supported reference path for the AgentGuard PDP and console.</p></div><h2>Reference topology</h2><p>The repository includes non-root Docker images and a minimal Kustomize base under <code>deploy/k8s</code>. The PDP owns policy evaluation and audit persistence; the console provides OIDC-protected operator workflows.</p><h2>Before rollout</h2><ol><li>Replace the example policy ConfigMap with reviewed schema and policies.</li><li>Create the chain-secret, API-key, and console OIDC secrets.</li><li>Terminate TLS at the ingress or service mesh and keep the PDP private.</li><li>Run an allow, deny, readiness, audit verification, and graceful shutdown smoke test.</li></ol><h2>Scaling boundary</h2><p>The shipped baseline uses one PDP and one console replica. The PDP audit volume is ReadWriteOnce. Configure the Redis-compatible console rate-limit store before scaling the console; coordinated append-only audit storage is still required for multi-replica PDP operation.</p><h2>Health and failure behavior</h2><p><code>/healthz</code> is liveness only. <code>/readyz</code> requires loaded policies and writable audit state. A configured audit append failure returns an error; a denial, timeout, malformed response, or unavailable PDP must never become implicit permission.</p><p>See the repository <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/docs/production.md">production runbook</a> for upgrade, rollback, storage, and secret handling details.</p></Docs>
